$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Pd-catalyzed Suzuki
coupling reactions. Pd-NHC catalyst 3 (0.5 mol%), base (1.5 mmol) and
aryl boronic acid (1 mmol) were weighed into a 50 mL glass vial that was
sealed with a septum and purged with N2 three times. Dioxane (2 mL) was
then injected via syringe followed by the aryl bromide (0.5 mmol) in
liquid case. If the aryl bromide was a solid, it was introduced into the
vial prior to purging with N2. At this time, the reaction stirred for 24
h at 80 °C. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and directly
purified via silica gel flash chromatography. 35: Yield 68%. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz, 298 K): δ =8.97 (s, 1H), 8.56 (d, J= 4.0 Hz,1H), 7.94
(d, J= 7.6Hz,1H), 7.84 (d,J= 7,6 Hz, 1H), 7.79 (d,J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.59
(s, 1H), 7.37-7.32 (m, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz, 298 K): δ =149.20,
147.50, 140.47, 140.30, 139.79, 133.65, 130.46, 124.97, 123.95, 123.79,
122.44, 120.86, 120.82.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Robust Acenaphthoimidazolylidene Palladium Complexes: Highly Efficient
Catalysts for Suzuki-Miyaura Couplings with Sterically Hindered
Substrates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tu, Tao; Sun, Zheming; Fang, Weiwei; Xu, Mizhi; Zhou, Yunfei
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(16), 4250-4253

