$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-chloro-N-(((3S,3aS)-1-oxo-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)thiophene-2-carbox
amide (24). A mixture of 23 (0.15 g, 0.34 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron
(0.13 g, 0.51 mmol), potassium acetate (0.10 g, 1.02 mmol) and
1,1-[bis-(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene]dichloropalladium(II)
dichloromethane complex (29 mg, 0.036 mmol) in DMSO (8 mL) was degassed
and flushed with argon. The mixture was heated at 80 °C for 2h. Ethyl
acetate (15 mL) was added, and the mixture was filtered through Celite,
washed with brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
The residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel with
petroleum/ethyl acetate (2:1) to afford of 24.
5-chloro-N-(((3S,3aR)-1-oxo-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1,3,3
a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]thiazin-3-yl)methyl)thiophene-2-carboxamide
(55a). Compound 55a (0.3 g, 68.0%) was prepared from 54a (0.4 g, 0.87
mmol) in the same manner as described for 24. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
8.99 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 1 H), 8.06-8.01 (m, 1 H), 7.69 (d, J = 4.1 Hz, 1 H),
7.42 (s, 1 H), 7.39 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1 H), 7.21 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.57
(d, J = 5.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.12 (dd, J = 12.9, 6.2 Hz, 1 H), 3.71 (s, 2 H),
3.30 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 2 H), 1.28 (s, 12 H). MS (EI) m/z: 506 (M+).
