$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure C: Catalytic Borylation A
flame-dried vial was charged with Fe(acac)3 (10 mol %) and B2pin2 (3.5
equiv) before evacuating and back-fing with N2. THF (0.2 M) was added,
followed by 10 mol % TMEDA (100 μL of a 4% (v/v) solution of TMEDA in
THF). Next, ethylmagnesium bromide (3M in Et2O, 4.5 equiv) was added
dropwise to the reaction mixture at a rate of one drop/sec. Finally,
substrate (1 equiv, generally 0.25 mmol or more) was added the reaction
mixture at once. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for
12h. Mixture was filtered through a plug of Celite over silica (1:5) with
multiple washes of Et2O (5 x 4 mL) and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The crude residue was purified by silica flash chromatography
(hexanes:EtOAc) to yield a colorless oil.
4,4,5,5-Tetramethy2-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (2gg).
4-Bromotetrahydro-2H-pyran 1gg (74.0 mg, 50.0 μL, 0.45 mmol) was treated
as per general Procedure C except with 20 mol % Fe(acac)3 (31.7 mg) and
20 mol % TMEDA (100 μL of 8% (v/v) TMEDA in THF) . Silica chromatography
(hexanes:EtOAc 95:5) yielded 2gg (63.6 mg, 67% yield) as a clear liquid.
TLC: Rf = 0.2 (hexanes:EtOAc 95:5) 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 3.85 - 3.70
(m, 2H), 3.52 - 3.35 (m, 2H), 1.67 - 1.50 (m, 4H), 1.23 (s, 1H), 1.21 (s,
12H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz): δ 83.2, 68.9, 27.7, 24.8. LRMS (EI)
Calcd. for C11H21BO3 [M], 212.16 . Found: 212.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iron-Catalyzed Borylation of Alkyl Electrophiles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Atack, Thomas C.; Lecker, Rachel M.; Cook, Silas P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2014), 136(27), 9521-9523

