$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.1. Synthesis of 1. To the solution of
4-iodophenol (1.1 g, 5 mmol) in toluene (25 mL), ethanol (25 mL),
5-formylthiophene-2-boronic acid (1.56 g, 10 mmol) and K3PO4·3H2O (2.67
g, 10 mmol) were added. Pd(OAc)2(58.4 mg, 0.6 mmol) was added under Ar.
The mixture was refluxed at 80°C for 8 h. After complete consumption of
the starting material, the solution was evaporated under reduced
pressure. The residual was purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
CH2Cl2 /CH3OH = 100:1, v/v). 3.7. Synthesis of 5. The synthesis procedure
is similar to that of 1. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, n-hexane/CH2Cl2 = 2/1, v/v) to give a red
solid (58.8 mg), yield 67.0%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.35 (d, 2H, J=
5.2 Hz), 7.24 (d, 2H, J= 8.6 Hz), 7.17 (d, 2H, J= 5.8 Hz), 7.09 (t, 2H,
J= 3.5 Hz), 6.86 (d, 2H, J= 3.5 Hz), 5.23 (s, 2H), 3.50 (s, 2H), 2.60 (s,
6H), 1.44 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 158.1, 155.1, 142.5,
140.8, 134.3, 131.6, 129.3, 128.3, 127.7, 127.2, 126.0, 171.0, 94.6,
56.2, 29.7, 13.5, 13.1. TOF HRMS ES+ (C29H27N2O2F2S2B): calcd 548.1575,
found 548.1577.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
