$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(S)-2-Imino-3,6-dimethyl-6-(5-(5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)thiophen-3-yl)tetrahydropyrimidin-4(1H)-one
(15). A heavy-walled glass vial was charged with (S)-tert-butyl
(4-(5-bromothiophen-3-yl)-1,4-dimethyl-6-oxotetrahydropyrimidin-2(1H)-ylidene)carbamate
F5 (46 mg, 0.11 mmol), (5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)boronic acid (33
mg, 0.21 mmol), tert-butanol (1.2 mL),
dichloro[1,1'-bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene]palladium(II)
dichloromethane complex (52 mg, 0.064 mmol), and aq. K2CO3 (2.0 M, 0.10
mL, 0.20 mmol). The vial was flushed with N2, sealed, and immersed in an
oil bath at 70 °C. The mixture was allowed to stir overnight, then cooled
to RT, filtered through a Celite plug and concentrated. The residue was
taken up in EtOAc, washed once each with water and brine, dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated to give (S)-tert-butyl
(1,4-dimethyl-6-oxo-4-(5-(5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)thiophen-3-yl)tetrahydropyrimidin-2(1H)-ylidene)carbamate
that was carried forward without further purification. The above material
was mixed with 10 mL of 25% (TFA with 5% water) in DCM and allowed to
stir at RT for 1.5 h. At that time, the mixture was concentrated and the
residue purified by RP-HPLC (Conditions C) to give
(S)-2-imino-3,6-dimethyl-6-(5-(5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)thiophen-3-yl)tetrahydropyrimidin-4(1H)-one
15. Yield 33 mg, 0.074 mmol, 67% 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 11.6 (s, 1H),
10.3 (br s, 1H), 8.86 (s, 1H), 8.55 (s, 1H), 8.20 (s, 1H), 7.54 (s, 1H),
7.28 (s, 1H), 3.32, 2.98 (ABq, J = 16.4 Hz, 2H), 3.27 (s, 3H), 2.12 (s,
3H), 1.75 (s, 3H). LCMS (Conditions B) tR = 3.23 min.; m/z 339.2 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM heavy-walled glass vial used and sealed (stage 1), Suzuki coupling (stage
1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of an Orally Available, Brain Penetrant BACE1 Inhibitor That
Affords Robust CNS Aβ Reduction
