$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To H1 (0.05 g, 0.11 mmol) in t-butanol (0.5 mL) was added
(5-(Prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)boronic acid (0.03 g, 0.21 mmol), 2M
K2CO3 (0.085 mL, 0.17 mmol), and PdCl2(dppf)-CH2Cl2 (0.019 g, 0.023
mmol). The reaction mixture was warmed to 65 °C and stirred for 3 h.
Water was added and the mixture was extracted with EtOAc. The combined
organic layers were washed with water and brine. The organic layer was
dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by preparative silica gel TLC (40% EtOAc/hex) to provide
(S)-tert-butyl
(4-(2-chloro-5-(5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)thiophen-3-yl)-1,4-dimethyl-6-oxotetrahydropyrimidin-2(1H)-ylidene)
carbamate. Yield 0.035 g, 67%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.5 (s, 1H),
8.55 (dd, J = 11.7, 2.2 Hz, 2H), 7.69 (m, 1H), 7.00 (s, 1H), 3.52, 2.85
(ABq, J = 16.1 Hz, 2 H), 3.24 (s, 3H), 2.11 (s, 3H), 1.79 (2, 3H), 1.55
(s, 9H). LCMS (Conditions B) tR = 4.79 min.; m/z 473.3 [M+H].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of an Orally Available, Brain Penetrant BACE1 Inhibitor That
Affords Robust CNS Aβ Reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Stamford, Andrew W.; Scott, Jack D.; Li, Sarah W.; Babu, Suresh; Tadesse,
Dawit; Hunter, Rachael; Wu, Yusheng; Misiaszek, Jeffrey; Cumming, Jared
N.; Gilbert, Eric J.; Huang, Chunli; McKittrick, Brian A.; Hong, Liwu;
Guo, Tao; Zhu, Zhaoning; Strickland, Corey; Orth, Peter; Voigt, Johannes
H.; Kennedy, Matthew E.; Chen, Xia; Kuvelkar, Reshma; Hodgson, Robert;
