$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Suzuki Coupling under
Microwave Conditions. 7-Acetamido-2-chloroquinoline-5,8-dione 8 (21 mg,
0.08 mmol) was dissolved in 4 mL of dimethoxyethane (DME) and degassed
under reduced pressure. Palladium(0) catalyst Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mg, 0084
mmol) was added and the solution was degassed further. The mixture was
stirred under Ar atmosphere for 10 minutes. Na2CO3 solution (0.2 mL, 2.0
M) was added, followed by boronic acid (0.126 mmol). The mixture was then
heated by use of a Biotage microwave initiator at 110-140 °C for 20
minutes. After cooling, TLC showed all the starting material was
consumed. The reaction mixture was poured into CH2Cl2 and washed with 2 ×
10 mL of water, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified on a HP-Sil 25 g Biotage SNAP
cartridge with EtOAc/heptane gradient (0-50%) at a flow rate of 20
mL/minutes. For very polar products, MeOH/CH2Cl2 (0-10% MeOH) was used as
solvent for purification.
7-Acetamido-2-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]quinoline-5,8-dione (9)
7-Acetamido-2-[2-(1-tert-butoxycarbonylindolyl)]quinoline-5,8-dione (12).
Yield: 63 mg (67%) of an orange solid was obtained. Rf = 0.40 (50%
EtOAc/heptane), mp 191-193 °C (decomp). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.47
(s, 1H), 8.45 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 8.15 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.97 (s,
1H), 7.89 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.60 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (t, J = 7.8
Hz, 1H), 7.27 (dd, J = 9.1, 5.9 Hz, 1H), 6.98 (s, 1H), 2.33 (s, 3H), 1.41
(s, 9H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 184.2, 179.0, 169.6, 157.4, 149.7,
145.3, 140.4, 138.1, 137.5, 134.2, 128.6, 127.9, 127.6, 126.0, 123.3,
121.5, 116.5, 115.2, 114.0, 84.2, 27.8, 25.1. HRMS (TOF MS ES+)
C24H22N3O5 + (MH+) calcd 432.1559, found 432.1568.
