$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
7-(2,3-O-Isopropylidene-5-O-tert-butyldimethylsilyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-4-phenyl-7H-pyrrolo[
2,3-d]pyrimidine (10d). An argon purged mixture of compound 8 (309 mg,
0.7 mmol), phenylboronic acid (128 mg, 1.05 mmol), K2CO3 (193 mg, 1.4
mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (41 mg, 0.035 mmol) in toluene (5 mL) was stirred at
100 °C for 5 h. The mixture was diluted with chloroform (20 mL) and
washed with aqueous NH4Cl (sat., 20 mL). The aqueous phase was
re-extracted with chloroform (2×5 mL) and the combined organic extracts
dried over MgSO4, concentrated in vacuo and the residue chromatographed
on silica (hexanes-AcOEt, 10:1→7:1) to afford 10d (320 mg, 95%) as a
colorless oil.
5-Fluoro-4-(thiophen-3-yl)-7-(2,3,5-tri-O-benzoyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-
d]pyrimidine (13n). Compound 13n was prepared as described for 10d by
coupling compound 12 and thiophene-3-boronic acid. A yellowish foam was
obtained after chromatography on silica (hexanes-AcOEt, 8:1). Yield 67%.
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): 4.69 (dd, 1H, J gem= 12.1, J 5´b,4´= 3.7,
H-5´b); 4.79 (ddd, 1H,J 4´,3´ = 4.2, J 4´,5´ = 3.7, 3.1, H- 4´); 4.88
(dd, 1H, J gem= 12.1,J 5´a,4´ = 3.1, H-5´a); 6.10 (dd, 1H, J 3´,2´ = 6.0,
J 3´,4´ = 4.2, H-3´); 6.16 (dd, 1H, J 2´,3´ J 2´,3´ = 6.0, J 2´,1´ = 5.9,
H-2´); 6.85 (dd, 1H, J 1´,2´ = 5.9, J H,F = 1.4, H-1´); 7.19 (d, 1H, J
H,F = 2.3, H-6); 7.36 (m, 2H, H-m-Bz); 7.42 (dd, 1H,J 5,4 = 5.1, J 5,2 =
3.0, H-5-thienyl); 7.42 and 7.50 (2 × m, 2 × 2H, H-m-Bz); 7.54, 7.59 and
7.62 (3 × m, 3 × 1H, H-p-Bz); 7.87 (ddd, 1H, J 4,5 = 5.1, J 4,2= 1.2, J
H,F = 0.8, H-4-thienyl); 7.94, 8.01 and 8.15 (3 × m, 3 × 2H, H-o- Bz);
8.23 (dd, 1H, J 2,5= 3.0,J 2,4 = 1.2, H-2-thienyl); 8.86 (s, 1H, H-2).
13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3): 63.77 (CH2-5´); 71.47 (CH-3´); 73.74 (CH-2´);
80.30 (CH-4´); 85.53 (CH-1´); 105.49 (d, J C,F = 15, C-4a); 108.23 (d, J
C,F = 31, CH-6); 125.89 (CH-5-thienyl); 128.08 (d,J C,F = 6,
CH-4-thienyl); 128.41 (C-i-Bz); 128.47, 128.54 and 128.71 (CH-m-Bz);
129.13 (d, J C,F = 11, CH-2-thienyl); 129.33 (C-i-Bz); 129.69, 129.83 and
129.84 (CH-o-Bz); 133.53 and 133.73 (CH-p-Bz); 139.02 (C-3-thienyl);
142.97 (d, J C,F = 251, C-5); 148.31 (d, J C,F = 3, C- 7a); 152.35
(CH-2); 152.94 (d, J C,F = 4, C-4); 165.11, 165.41 and 166.14 (CO). 19F
NMR (470.3 MHz, CDCl3): -154.62. MS FAB, m/z (rel. %): 664 (100)[M+H]. HR
MS (FAB): calcd for C36H27FN3O7S [M+H] 664.1554, found 664.1552.
