$DATUM (S)-3-chloro-1-fluoro-7-(2-fluoropyridin-3-yl)-5'H-spiro[chromeno[2,3-c]pyridine-5,4'-oxazol]-2'-amine
(7s). A mixture of
(S)-7-bromo-3-chloro-1-fluoro-5'H-spiro[chromeno[2,3-c]pyridine-5,4'-oxazol]-2'-amine
(40.0 mg, 0.104 mmol), pyridin-3-ylboronic acid (21.73 mg, 0.177 mmol),
bis-(di-tert-butyl(4-dimethylaminophenyl)phosphine)dichloropalladium(ii)
(2.95 mg, 4.16 μmol) and potassium phosphate (66.2 mg, 0.312 mmol) in 1.5
ml of dioxane/water = 2:1 was heated at 120 °C microwave for 20 min. LCMS
showed mostly conversion to the mono coupling product. 10 mg of
pyridin-3-ylboronic acid (21.73 mg, 0.177 mmol) was added and the
reaction was heated at 140 °C under microwave for 20 min. The reaction
mixture was directly loaded to column chromatography (SiO2, DCM to
DCM/MeOH = 100:1 to 100:6) to give crude final product which was further
purified by prep TLC (DCM/MeOH).
1-fluoro-3,7-di(pyridin-3-yl)-5'H-spiro[chromeno[2,3-c]pyridine-5,4'-oxazol]-2'-amine
as a white solid. MS m/z = (M+1): 401.0. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ ppm
8.25 (dt, J=4.69, 1.60 Hz, 1 H) 8.12 (ddd, J=10.07, 7.73, 1.76 Hz, 1 H)
7.65 (dt, J=8.61, 1.60 Hz, 1 H) 7.58 (t, J=1.60 Hz, 1 H) 7.49 (ddd,
J=7.09, 5.04, 1.76 Hz, 1 H) 7.42 (d, J=8.41 Hz, 1 H) 7.25 (s, 1 H) 6.69
(s, 2 H) 4.38 (d, J=8.80 Hz, 1 H) 4.24 (d, J=8.80 Hz, 1 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Orally Available BACE1 Inhibitor That Affords Robust CNS Aβ Reduction
without Cardiovascular Liabilities
